## Why the start determinant is optional

G3CK constructs a rational selected-source cyclic frame on

```text
0<t<=1,
```

but leaves its algebraic start value `Delta_Kr(1)` open. That boundary matters
only if one insists that a single cyclic companion frame include `t=0`. It is
not a boundary for the full transport problem.

G3BK proves that every pole of the fixed H20, H11 and H02 parent charts is
algebraic. The G3BJ interior is transcendental and therefore avoids every
such pole. The B89 charts are units at `a=0`, and G3BN/G3BR together with the
G3BK H20 endpoint certificate prove all parent charts are units at `a=1`.

Consequently the fixed augmented B103/Macaulay coordinate frame is regular on
the complete selected path

```text
0<=t<=1.
```

It is a computational frame, not a claimed horizontal or integral frame.

## Two-gauge atlas

Use the following two frames:

```text
U_std = [0,1] : fixed 1510-dimensional augmented B103 frame,
U_cyc = (0,1] : G3CK selected-source affine Krylov frame B_aff(a).
```

On their overlap, G3CK gives

```text
B_aff(a) in GL_1510(Q(gamma)(a)).
```

The exact coordinate transitions are

```text
Y = B_aff(a) q,
q = B_aff(a)^-1 Y.
```

Initial data may therefore be imposed at `t=0` in `U_std`. The calculation may
remain in that frame for the whole path or switch to `U_cyc` at any certified
point with `t>0`. No value of `Delta_Kr(1)` is needed for either option.

## Equations in the two frames

The standard-frame equation is

```text
Y_dot=a'(t) K_tilde(a(t))Y.
```

The cyclic-frame equation is

```text
q_dot=a'(t)[C_aff(a(t))-Omega_aff(a(t))]q,
Omega_aff=B_aff^-1 dB_aff/da.
```

They are related by the displayed transition and are exactly equivalent on
the overlap. This is a gauge atlas, not a transport-dimension reduction.

## Frontier consequence

Computing the large start-fiber Krylov determinant would still be useful if a
single companion chart is desired, but it is no longer a prerequisite. The
actual blocker is the coefficient/action layer:

1. emit a characteristic-zero or certified interval action oracle for the
   selected full connection along G3BJ;
2. in the standard frame, complete the H02 pole-six and recursive action for
   the evolving selected state, reusing G3BO/G3BT and the rank-6,022 update;
3. integrate with the exact factor `a'(t)`;
4. certify the terminal integral marking and normalized 248-row readout.

G3CL does not emit that action, perform the integration, identify the
computational frame with the integral local system, or decide `beta_C`.

